   "text": "The drawing shows Fmoc\u2011His(Boc)\u2011OH, the L\u2011histidine derivative with both protecting groups.\n\n- **Imidazole ring:** the ring nitrogen at lower left carries the Boc group (N\u2013C(=O)OC(C)(C)C). The other ring nitrogen is the unsubstituted =N\u2013. The CH2 side chain sits on the ring carbon next to that =N\u2013, which gives the pattern c1cn(Boc)cn1.\n- **Side chain and \u03b1\u2011carbon:** the ring carbon connects through CH2 to the \u03b1\u2011carbon, which carries CO2H on a wedge bond and NH\u2013Fmoc on a plain bond.\n- **Fmoc:** NC(=O)OCC1c2ccccc2-c2ccccc21 (the fluorenylmethyl carbamate).\n- **Stereochemistry:** the implicit hydrogen points back, and the sequence N \u2192 CO2H \u2192 CH2 runs counterclockwise, so the centre is S, which is the L configuration. Writing the \u03b1\u2011carbon as [C@H] with the neighbour order C(=O)O, H, CH2, N reproduces this.\n\nSMILES: OC(=O)[C@H](Cc1cn(C(=O)OC(C)(C)C)cn1)NC(=O)OCC1c2ccccc2-c2ccccc21"
